   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to validate certain acts of the Fredonia central school district with regard to a certain capital improvement project",
    "basePrintNo": "S7681",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7681-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7681\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to validate certain acts of the Fredonia central school\ndistrict with regard to a certain capital improvement project\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThe purpose of this legislation is to authorize the Fredonia Central\nSchool District to receive state aid for a certain approved capital\nfunded project.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Directors that the capital improvement project number\n06-22-01-06-009-008 is in fact eligible for state aid.\n\nSection 2: Legalizes act pertinent to the project and directs that\npayment shall be made pursuant to the New York State Education Law.\n\nSection 3: States that the State Education Department is directed to\nconsider the approved cost as valid and proper obligations of the\nFredonia Central School District.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Fredonia Central School District, unfortunately, neglected to file\nthe Final Cost Reports for a building project with the Office of\nFacility Planning within the established time frame.  Requiring the\nschool district to pay back or have it not receive the anticipated\nstate aid for the projects would be devastating to the school\ndistrict.  This legislation would allow the Education Department to\nconsider the final cost report legalized, validated, ratified and\nconfirmed.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nFormerly, S.868-A of 2009, Vetoed by the Governor.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for the State since\nthe state aid has already been approved and budgeted.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
